{
  "concept": "The fluid force on a vertically submerged flat surface is built up as a Riemann sum of thin horizontal strips, each carrying force ρ·h(x*ₖ)·w(x*ₖ)·Δxₖ, whose limit is the integral F = ∫ₐᵇ ρ h(x) w(x) dx.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Downward-pointing vertical depth axis on the left of each panel, arrowhead at bottom, tick marks with labels",
    "Wavy black line at the top of each panel representing the fluid surface",
    "Light-blue vertical gradient fill behind everything (pale at surface, deeper blue with depth) suggesting increasing pressure with depth",
    "Irregular closed blob (kidney/bean shaped) filled pale orange with a black outline — the submerged plate, same silhouette in all three panels",
    "Panel (a): red dashed horizontal lines at depths a (top of plate) and b (bottom of plate), labeled 'a' and 'b' on the axis",
    "Panel (a): horizontal teal segment across the blob at depth x with black dots at both endpoints, labeled w(x)",
    "Panel (a): double-headed vertical arrow at the right from the fluid surface down to level x, labeled h(x)",
    "Panel (a): axis tick and label 'x' at the strip level",
    "Panel (a) caption '(a)'",
    "Panel (b): partition ticks labeled a = x₀, x₁, x₂, x₃, vertical dots, x_{n−1}, b = xₙ on the depth axis",
    "Panel (b): red dashed lines from each partition tick to the blob, continuing as teal horizontal chords across the blob",
    "Panel (b): strip labels A₁, A₂, A₃, vertical ellipsis, Aₙ placed inside the corresponding bands",
    "Panel (b) caption '(b)'",
    "Panel (c): close-up of the kth strip — the blob with a green-tinted rectangle spanning its width at the k-th band",
    "Panel (c): axis labels a, x_{k−1}, x*ₖ (with dot on axis), xₖ, b; red dashed line at x*ₖ across the rectangle with black endpoint dots",
    "Panel (c): vertical double-headed arrow at the right edge of the rectangle labeled Δxₖ",
    "Panel (c): long vertical double-headed arrow from fluid surface to x*ₖ labeled h(x*ₖ)",
    "Panel (c): horizontal double-headed arrow with end bars below the rectangle labeled w(x*ₖ)",
    "Panel (c) caption '(c)'",
    "Formula annotation panel: F ≈ Σ ρ h(x*ₖ) w(x*ₖ) Δxₖ  →  F = ∫ₐᵇ ρ h(x) w(x) dx",
    "Numeric readout box showing current n, the Riemann-sum force estimate, the exact integral value, and the percent error"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "panelView",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "View",
      "options": ["(a) whole plate", "(b) n strips", "(c) kth strip detail", "All three panels", "Single animated panel"],
      "default": "All three panels",
      "teaches": "That the three textbook panels are three zoom levels of one argument: the continuous plate, its partition, and the single representative strip."
    },
    {
      "id": "nStrips",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Number of strips n",
      "range": [1, 60, 1],
      "default": 8,
      "teaches": "That refining the partition makes each rectangular strip hug the curved boundary and drives the Riemann sum toward the exact integral value of the fluid force."
    },
    {
      "id": "stripIndex",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Strip index k",
      "range": [1, 60, 1],
      "default": 3,
      "teaches": "That each strip contributes its own force ρ·h(x*ₖ)·w(x*ₖ)·Δxₖ — deep strips contribute more per unit area because h grows, while contribution also tracks the local width w."
    },
    {
      "id": "accumulate",
      "type": "animation",
      "label": "Accumulate strip forces top → bottom",
      "loop": false,
      "teaches": "That the total force is literally the running sum of the strip forces, accumulating fastest where the plate is both wide and deep.",
      "...": ""
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The whole submerged plate",
      "narration": "A flat plate hangs vertically in the fluid between depths a and b. At any depth x it has width w(x) and lies under depth h(x) of fluid — but pressure is not constant over the plate, so force is not just pressure × area.",
      "state": { "panelView": "(a) whole plate", "nStrips": 1 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Slice it into horizontal strips",
      "narration": "Partition the depth interval a = x₀ < x₁ < … < xₙ = b. Each horizontal band Aₖ is thin enough that the depth — and therefore the pressure — barely changes across it.",
      "state": { "panelView": "(b) n strips", "nStrips": 8 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Zoom in on the kth strip",
      "narration": "Pick a sample depth x*ₖ inside [x_{k−1}, xₖ]. Approximate the strip by a rectangle of width w(x*ₖ) and height Δxₖ, sitting at uniform depth h(x*ₖ), so its force is ρ·h(x*ₖ)·w(x*ₖ)·Δxₖ.",
      "state": { "panelView": "(c) kth strip detail", "nStrips": 8, "stripIndex": 4 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Walk down the plate",
      "narration": "Slide k from top to bottom and watch h(x*ₖ) grow steadily while w(x*ₖ) rises and falls with the shape. Deep, wide strips dominate the total force.",
      "state": { "panelView": "All three panels", "nStrips": 8, "stripIndex": 7 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Add up the strips",
      "narration": "Accumulating the strip forces from the surface downward builds the Riemann sum F ≈ Σ ρ h(x*ₖ) w(x*ₖ) Δxₖ; the running total climbs fastest through the widest, deepest part of the plate.",
      "state": { "panelView": "Single animated panel", "nStrips": 8, "stripIndex": 8 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Refine the partition",
      "narration": "Raise n and the rectangles fill the blob almost exactly; the sum settles onto the exact value F = ∫ₐᵇ ρ h(x) w(x) dx and the error readout collapses toward zero.",
      "state": { "panelView": "Single animated panel", "nStrips": 48, "stripIndex": 24 }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Because pressure grows with depth, force must be summed depth-band by depth-band — each thin strip is a nearly-constant-pressure rectangle, and the limit of those strip forces is exactly the integral ∫ₐᵇ ρ h(x) w(x) dx.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Three stacked panels sharing one visual language, each on a pale-to-deeper blue vertical gradient with a black wavy fluid surface across the top. A downward black arrow serves as the depth axis on the left of every panel — depth increases downward, so labels read a above b. The plate is one irregular kidney/bean-shaped blob with a smooth black outline and pale orange fill, reused identically in all panels. Chords across the blob are thin teal lines; partition/level indicator lines running from the axis to the blob are dashed red; endpoint markers are solid black dots. Panel (a) adds a double-headed h(x) arrow on the right from the wavy surface down to level x, and labels w(x) inside the blob. Panel (b) stacks many teal chords with dashed red leaders to ticks a = x₀ … b = xₙ, strip names A₁, A₂, A₃, ⋮, Aₙ set in the bands, and vertical ellipses on both the axis and inside the blob. Panel (c) is the zoomed strip: a green-tinted rectangle spanning the blob's full width at that band, a red dashed line at x*ₖ through it, a small Δxₖ arrow at the right edge, a long h(x*ₖ) arrow to the surface, and a w(x*ₖ) measurement arrow with end bars below. Interactive additions: the currently selected strip should glow (saturated orange/green) in panel (b) and drive panel (c); a small readout box near the caption area shows n, Σ ρ h w Δx, the exact integral, and % error, with the formula F ≈ Σ ρ h(x*ₖ) w(x*ₖ) Δxₖ → F = ∫ₐᵇ ρ h(x) w(x) dx displayed beneath. Panel captions (a), (b), (c) in italic serif below each panel."
}

